     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended amlodipine dose for adults is 10 mg once daily. Usual doses are 2.5\u201310 mg. A 50 mg dose is five times the maximum. It could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. This is true even with normal kidney and liver function. The dose may be a typo, for example 5 mg.\n\n2. **You're not a prescriber.** Medication orders need to come from a licensed clinician who can verify the indication and dose. The prescriber should enter the order or confirm it with me directly.\n\nIf the prescriber meant a standard dose, such as 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily, ask them to confirm the intended dose. I can enter it once I have that confirmation. If 50 mg really was intended, it needs to be verified with the prescriber and pharmacy before anything is entered."
      }
