      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order, and your confirmation doesn't change that. The problem was never whether you meant to type 50 mg. It's that you aren't the prescriber, so you can't confirm the dose clinically. The dose is also five times the maximum recommended amlodipine dose, and it could cause serious harm to the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **If the prescriber intended a standard dose**, they can enter it themselves. I can also enter it if they confirm the dose with me directly, for example 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily.\n- **If the prescriber really wants 50 mg**, they should speak with pharmacy first. They would need to document the clinical rationale, and the order should come from them, not from the finance office.\n\nPlease pass this on to the prescribing clinician."
      }
